{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1793654965002973002,"compiled_state":{"alias":"crumbly-amphibole-smelts","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":5,"unsigned":1},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"35f66b4c01e61534d80e1b5aadd1379cf39078ed2dec637ade490ba68c790cfa","event_uuid":"a37c4476-ee75-4e0d-bde7-c36f3e7b3f91","position":{"commit_sha":"30ec7a26c31205abd351501e02a37233ee4b13a1","position":"1793647918651154327-a37c4476-ee75-4e0d-bde7-c36f3e7b3f91"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"dc2b48c28392262a470e3758d98159d4acd9ff354930ddaba3bac6cfe0de1d3d","event_uuid":"2325ffab-944d-4f7e-a08a-afd9035dcce0","position":{"commit_sha":"6b8656307cd3079ef0ec80ca18871ff2d505f34b","position":"1793649637301860931-2325ffab-944d-4f7e-a08a-afd9035dcce0"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"fc687c4f31070e03d00ecfd9739f72b9740fbc0f2dc36a7dd29bc63cf6b4ef96","event_uuid":"dc41db99-f428-4327-9bd6-1721b79b11b4","position":{"commit_sha":"b661bfed9467bb5766e3dde50d5d27c6fc78d4fb","position":"1793653629143949097-dc41db99-f428-4327-9bd6-1721b79b11b4"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"18cf4fed02217f958022a65a419d1507a6726dd0f9785a12f346b5fb2d77c1b1","event_uuid":"d3a8acc3-d316-4116-95be-b9640fc47ff3","position":{"commit_sha":"0efb96c3f5d6aebb6b5b51ce91cc85d022070846","position":"1793654167070063448-d3a8acc3-d316-4116-95be-b9640fc47ff3"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"898fe3f8b5d30225dac0160cb033dc732b00ce113229c737ba4dc13ee5f78244","event_uuid":"82982fb0-a122-4487-b42f-ad671691a544","position":{"commit_sha":"c9fa66d34c2c468c3b3a43123817d56910bfafaf","position":"1793654738116473752-82982fb0-a122-4487-b42f-ad671691a544"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1793647918651154327,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[],"description":"## Parent\n\nEpic `77e3-28e2-31ec-47ec`, authorized at full scope by the operator on 2026-11-02.\nDeliverable 1. The net-mechanism red proof (deliverable 3's half) is the calibration\ncorpus, split into a child because carrying both exceeds the 8,000-character admission cap\n`verify.max_ticket_description_chars`. Citations below were measured individually rather\nthan sampled: `scripts/` and `src/` line numbers from `origin/main` `4cf1ae42946`, the\n`.rebar/` overlay line numbers from the working tree at that base.\n\n## The gap\n\n`scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py` is a shrink-only ratchet over\n`.github/mechanism-baseline.json` censusing seven mechanism kinds, admitting a new one by\nan in-tree marker `# mechanism-ok: <kind> <name> — <reason>`. A `new` key with a nonblank\nmarker passes at `scripts/_mechanism_delta/compare.py:89-92`, and the marker grammar\n`_MARKER_RE` at `scripts/_mechanism_delta/markers.py:20` has exactly three fields — kind,\nname, reason. Nothing parses a retirement.\n\nSo the ratchet asks \"is this mechanism justified?\", never \"is the system net-simpler\nafterward?\". Plan review does not close the gap either — `A1` is the only complexity\ncriterion and is advisory, at `\"block_threshold\": 0.95` / `\"default_posture\": \"advisory\"`\n(`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/criteria_routing.json:814-815`).\n\nThis change adds a BLOCKING plan-review criterion, `project.net-mechanism`: a plan adding a\nmechanism of a counted kind must either name the mechanism it retires or state why no\nretirement is possible, and blocks absent both. It reasons about the PLAN, not the tree —\nit runs at claim time, before any code exists.\n\n## Route: project overlay, not a packaged criterion\n\n`project.portability` is a BLOCKING criterion living entirely in the overlay:\n`.rebar/criteria_routing.json:3-14` (posture `blocking`, threshold 0.9, `exec: 1-TURN`),\nits `activate` entry at `:130-132`, a rubric under `.rebar/prompts/`, a corpus under\n`.rebar/evals/`, and ABSENT from `CANONICAL_LLM` (`registry.py:87`). Five overlay\nplan-review criteria ship this way, so the route has precedent.\n\nChosen because the trigger is rebar's own seven-kind census, which a downstream consumer\ndoes not have: a packaged criterion would fire on their plans. REJECTED, recorded so it is\nnot re-litigated — a packaged criterion in `CANONICAL_LLM`, which additionally costs edits\nto `check_registry_coverage` (`registry.py:536`), `validate_packaged_routing()`\n(`registry.py:564`) and the regenerated guide (`criteria_guide.py:89`), inviting `A1` on a\ncomplexity-reduction deliverable.\n\n## The rubric's decision logic\n\nThe criterion carries no code — its behaviour IS the rubric body, so the body is specified\nhere rather than left to the implementer. Section structure is measured from\n`.rebar/prompts/plan-review-project-portability.md`.\n\n**Self-contained taxonomy.** The criterion never reads the ratchet script or the baseline:\nit runs at claim time against plan prose with no tree access, so it has no runtime source\nfor the taxonomy. The rubric body must ENUMERATE the closed seven-kind list inline —\n`lock`, `env_var`, `config_key`, `feature_flag`, `ci_gate`, `autouse_fixture`,\n`test_helper` — each with a one-line cue for recognising it in plan prose, and must state\nthat the list is closed: an element matching none of the seven is not this criterion's\nconcern. That judgment belongs to `A1`.\n\n**Detection heuristic.** The reviewer extracts, from the plan's stated edit set, every\nelement it proposes to ADD matching a listed kind and every element it proposes to REMOVE\nmatching one. An addition is recognised from the plan's declarative statements about what\nit will create, not from speculation about what the implementation might need.\n\n**Finding threshold** (modeled on `plan-review-project-portability.md:17-37`, which\nrequires all four of its named elements before emitting). Emit only when ALL of: (1) the\nplan adds at least one element of a listed kind; (2) it names no element of those kinds it\nwill retire; (3) it carries no explicit statement of why no retirement is possible; (4) the\naddition is specific enough to name a kind and a name. Condition 4 stops the criterion\nmanufacturing findings from underspecified plans — underspecification is another\ncriterion's subject.\n\n**Required finding fields** (modeled on `plan-review-project-portability.md:39-54`): five\ntyped fields — `location` (the plan section proposing the addition), `finding` (the kind\nand name added, plus the absence of both retirement and justification), `mechanisms` (the\nadded kind/name pairs), `evidence` (quoted plan text), `criteria`.\n\n**Non-findings.** Do NOT emit for: a plan retiring more than it adds; a plan naming a\nretirement, even in a different kind; a plan stating why no retirement is possible,\nwhatever the reviewer thinks of that reasoning — the criterion checks the justification is\nPRESENT, not persuasive, since judging persuasiveness would make it non-reproducible; a\nplan adding no mechanism; a plan adding complexity outside the seven kinds.\n\n## Where firing behaviour is proven, and why blocking is safe meanwhile\n\nNot here. `tests/unit/test_project_portability_criterion.py` never executes model judgment,\nso a unit test claiming \"this plan is scored as a finding\" could only assert a canned\nscore — proving the fixture, not the criterion. This ticket's tests are therefore\nSTRUCTURAL ONLY; firing behaviour lives in the child's corpus.\n\nThe criterion consequently goes live blocking before its firing behaviour is measured. That\nis safe because the finding threshold is CONJUNCTIVE: all four conditions must hold, and\ncondition 2 is satisfied by any plan naming a retirement. An uncalibrated rubric of that\nshape fails by staying SILENT rather than blocking plans it should pass. The child proves\nit fires when it should.\n\n## Files this change touches\n\n1. `.rebar/prompts/plan-review-project-net-mechanism.md` — NEW, the rubric above; front\n   matter is the six keys `parse_front_matter` reads.\n2. `.rebar/criteria_routing.json` — a routing entry plus an `activate` entry.\n3. `tests/unit/test_project_net_mechanism_criterion.py` — NEW, structural only.\n\nThe rubric filename is derived, not chosen: `src/rebar/llm/criteria/ids.py:42` computes\n`f\"{prefix}{criterion_id.replace('.', '-')}\"`. `scripts/check_criteria_vocabulary.py`\nscans only `src/rebar/llm/reviewers` and `src/rebar/_guides` (`:56`), so this overlay\nrubric needs no allowlist row.\n\n## Portability and provider neutrality\n\nThe criterion runs inside plan review, an in-process operation-linked path: it reads plan\ntext, never the CI environment and never the ratchet script, so it behaves identically with\nno CI provider configured. The `ci_gate` kind concerns what the PLAN says it will add —\nrecognising \"a new required check\" in prose needs no CI present. The rubric is\n`exec: 1-TURN`, names no vendor, and needs no model-specific capability.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\nEach names one deliverable; none bundles two with \"and\". All are structural, in\n`tests/unit/test_project_net_mechanism_criterion.py` except the last.\n\n- [ ] `registry.effective_criteria(REPO_ROOT)` contains `project.net-mechanism`.\n- [ ] `effective_routing(REPO_ROOT)[\"project.net-mechanism\"][\"default_posture\"]` is\n      `\"blocking\"`.\n- [ ] `prompts.get_prompt(criterion_prompt_id(\"project.net-mechanism\"), repo_root=REPO_ROOT)`\n      returns a non-empty body.\n- [ ] `parse_front_matter` on that body yields all six keys.\n- [ ] `route_criteria` returns `project.net-mechanism` for a plan in its declared scope.\n- [ ] The rubric body contains a `## Finding threshold` heading.\n- [ ] The rubric body contains a `## Required finding fields` heading.\n- [ ] The rubric body contains a `## Non-findings` heading.\n- [ ] The rubric body names all seven kinds as literal strings.\n- [ ] The rubric body contains none of `GitHub Actions`, `GitLab`, `Jenkins`, `CircleCI`,\n      `Travis`.\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":".rebar/prompts/plan-review-project-net-mechanism.md","reason":"NEW - the criterion rubric, modeled on plan-review-project-portability.md"},{"path":".rebar/criteria_routing.json","reason":"Add the project.net-mechanism routing entry and activate it"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_project_net_mechanism_criterion.py","reason":"NEW - structural contract test over the committed .rebar/ overlay; runs no model"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["parent","77e3-28e2-31ec-47ec"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"77e3-28e2-31ec-47ec","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["complexity-reduction"],"ticket_id":"fe94-2e22-ea9e-46f7","ticket_type":"story","title":"Add a blocking net-mechanism plan-review criterion: adding a mechanism must name what it retires","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["a37c4476-ee75-4e0d-bde7-c36f3e7b3f91","2325ffab-944d-4f7e-a08a-afd9035dcce0","dc41db99-f428-4327-9bd6-1721b79b11b4","d3a8acc3-d316-4116-95be-b9640fc47ff3","82982fb0-a122-4487-b42f-ad671691a544","18297c02-1b06-4454-b64e-71015e9aeada"]},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1793654965002973002,"uuid":"87db48d9-cdc4-407d-bac5-eca850ccc712"}